  "body": "https://wicg.github.io/BackgroundSync/spec/PeriodicBackgroundSync-index.html has a couple terms, like [minimum periodic sync interval for any origin](https://wicg.github.io/BackgroundSync/spec/PeriodicBackgroundSync-index.html#minimum-periodic-sync-interval-for-any-origin), that it currently defines as \"a long long [number of milliseconds]\". However, this number isn't exposed to Javascript anywhere, so it doesn't really need a particular data type other than being an interval of time. It might be easier to get specs like this right if Infra defined [types](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#primitive-data-types) for points in time and amounts of time.",
